"CONSTRAINT LAWS over a literal carrier with the compile`s records. V is exactly: the two rows giving p1 two Names (uniqueness within Person has Name); the two joined rows giving p2 and p3 one Name and Age (the external uniqueness); p4, who has no Age (the explicit mandatory); the reflexive row (irreflexive) and the three rows the asymmetric ring breaks, not the row whose reverse is absent; and p4 again, happy with no Age (the subset). The disjunctive mandatory holds, since every Person is happy or likes some Person. The subset with a join recipe and the prohibited deontics are listed as unbuilt; the one the compile gives by a recipe spans no role, where the one by its role spans one. The instance reflection, not yet booted, holds p4 an instance of Person and most specifically of Happy Person, the derived subtype its rule gives it, and p2 most specifically of Person, Ann one of Name, and p1 none of Name. The schema reflected: Person has Name has its primary reading rPersonHasName and its roles are used in it; Person has PersonId, named in state:mapinputs alone, is declared with its roles and players; Person has Age has no third role. The involvement link Person is involved in Person likes Person, named in state:mapinputs alone with no template, has its reading with NORMA`s text and its Predicate; Person has PersonId, templated by its reference mode (k:schemereadings), gets no minted text. Person likes Person objectified, the link reads p2 involved in the instance p2.p3, and not p3; Person meets Person, filed and objectified but declared with no roles, gives its link no row, the player having no role there to read. The rules read on read: Person, a subtype of Party, has each instance x of its own as <x, x> in Person is a subtype of Party, and Ann, a Name, none; Person`s popular reference mode reads Person has PersonId <x, x> for each Person; the objectified instance p2.p3, reached through its link, is an instance of Person likes Person. The recipes: Person reaches Person is the closure of likes, p1 reaching p3 and p3 not p1, seven rows; the age band pairs each Person of age 30 with thirty; the sad are the named less the happy; Happy Person, a derived subtype, holds p4 and not p2; Person counts Person, which would introduce a value on its own cycle, is refused: RULES gives it no rule, where it gives the closure one. Within one V the closure`s rows, bound once, are what reading it answers; Person reaches Person, derived and objectified with a link, gives no instance of its own, where Person likes Person, filed, does. Instance-of read as its rule: p4 is an instance of Person, Party and Happy Person, p2 not of Happy Person, Ann of Name, p9 of Band as P asserts, and p2.p3 of Person likes Person. The Domains: Person is declared in both people and crm, and Person has Name in people; each declared name is its own Local Name, once.",
